From 8ae2509c10b82770a4652893931363f00d184cc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:38:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LOOM-8: generators. A melodic track can have a generator per
 pattern, EUCLID or TURING (ARP's last page, Generator): it plays a live copy
 of the track's steps, shown on the grid and the white-key LEDs as it changes,
 and leaves the stored pattern as it was until COMMIT GENERATOR (SEL list;
 undoable) writes it in. A hit on a step with notes plays them with the
 generated velocity, on an empty step the root (the pattern's first note, else
 C4); the step's tricks and chance stay. EUCLID: length, hits, rotate. TURING:
 a 2..16 bit shift register that starts from the pattern's steps, lock (0
 random .. 127 the loop repeats exactly), density, velocity from the register.
 It composes with the random player (rhythm from the generator, pitch from the
 pool). The settings live in a pseudo-lane (LANE_GEN), no format change; the
 shadow is 64 bytes a track in RAM. generator.xy (expect gen, expect genhits);
 t_generators; the manual

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
